My videos are being watched everywhere.

240
00:15:37,616 --> 00:15:37,977
So glad.

241
00:15:38,057 --> 00:15:42,920
I'm an avid follower of your Ask Ganji Sohaq series and sincerely applaud your work.

242
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:43,470
Thank you.

243
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:47,470
I wish God keeps you and your family in good health and happiness and so do you.

244
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:54,712
My problem is pretty basic but I believe your approach might be more insightful than an average person from society.

245
00:15:54,792 --> 00:15:57,060
I'm 27 and my graduation took almost 8 years.

246
00:15:57,140 --> 00:16:02,340
to complete due to a mandatory rural service born after MBBS in my state.

247
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,808
My college was in a suburb,

248
00:16:04,888 --> 00:16:10,370
but growing up I always had big city dreams and I wanted to explore different places and cultures,

249
00:16:10,450 --> 00:16:12,820
travel, learn Kathak and classical singing.

250
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:15,364
Due to lack of guidance,

251
00:16:15,444 --> 00:16:18,995
I couldn't choose a career which helped me do the above activities,

252
00:16:19,075 --> 00:16:23,890
but fortunately I'm a pretty skilled doctor as well and I genuinely enjoy my work and have kept.

253
00:16:23,970 --> 00:16:30,530
kept other activities aside as a hobby. Since my rural bond is over now, I finally feel free

254
00:16:30,610 --> 00:16:43,259
to live my life on my own terms and planning to do further studies in a relatively lighter branch of medicine which allows me enough time to enjoy other beautiful treasures this journey of life has to offer.

255
00:16:43,339 --> 00:16:46,817
But then this marriage thing came in between.

256
00:16:46,897 --> 00:16:50,770
My family wishes me to get married, but they aren't forcing me yet.

257
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:57,260
I completely understand where they are coming from. I also want to get married and have a family someday.

258
00:16:57,600 --> 00:17:01,104
But I'm not sure if that day comes this year or anytime soon.

259
00:17:01,184 --> 00:17:01,484
Also,

260
00:17:01,564 --> 00:17:08,180
I think I'm thinking of getting married just because of pressure of getting near expiry date for bearing children.

261
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:12,180
Is there any way I can find a middle ground and do not have to choose one over another?

262
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:18,770
Also, I've been in two relationships so far. First one was at a very immature age, so it doesn't even count. In the second, I'm…

263
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:22,310
Second, I invested a lot but got cheated on twice.

264
00:17:22,390 --> 00:17:24,610
Breakup was one of the toughest times I experienced.

265
00:17:24,690 --> 00:17:29,746
I realized even after being in a long distance for most parts of the relationship,

266
00:17:29,826 --> 00:17:32,030
I was emotionally addicted to this guy.

267
00:17:32,110 --> 00:17:37,160
I experienced lack of affection from parents in childhood, which made me really needy.

268
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:42,204
I literally used to have panic attacks like symptoms every night around 9 p.m.

269
00:17:42,284 --> 00:17:44,350
which was our usual time of call.

270
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:46,510
He was also attached to me but.

271
00:17:46,590 --> 00:17:51,230
For me, he was the center of my universe. Maybe I even overburdened him because of this.

272
00:17:52,430 --> 00:17:58,110
Ironically enough, I was this strong independent woman in others' eyes because I would do every

273
00:17:58,190 --> 00:18:03,390
other every work of mine without his help. But whenever I faced any kind of emotional issues, I

274
00:18:03,470 --> 00:18:07,790
would run straight to him. Anyways, later I took therapy and started to heal and forgive him

275
00:18:07,870 --> 00:18:12,750
without getting back together. It's been a year and I'm trying best to move on.

276
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:19,760
Although I've come a long way, but after past experience, getting dependent on humans has started to scare me.

277
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:23,022
I'm not scared of relationships and falling in love,

278
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:28,510
but I don't want my life to center around that as well like it was the last time.

279
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:33,440
I want to know how to be vulnerable yet strong in relationships.

280
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:37,116
I just don't want to experience the pain I did this time.

281
00:18:37,196 --> 00:18:40,430
God forbid something similar happens in the future.

282
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:46,550
I've tried medication. I would like to know if you have any other solution for the same. Thank you for reading.

283
00:18:46,630 --> 00:18:51,910
So basically, she's a 27-year-old doctor who lives in an Indian village.

284
00:18:52,030 --> 00:18:55,259
In India, there's a rule, perhaps in her state,

285
00:18:55,339 --> 00:18:58,374
that the doctor has to serve for two years.

286
00:18:58,454 --> 00:19:00,790
I think they call it a rural bond.

287
00:19:00,870 --> 00:19:07,030
So she did that and… rural service bond. Okay.

288
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:12,220
She wants to explore, travel, learn Kathak and classical singing.

289
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:14,220
But now, obviously, she has a pressure from home.

290
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:18,620
The pressure is not good, but she is being forced to do it.

291
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:22,851
And it's not like she doesn't want to settle down,

292
00:19:22,931 --> 00:19:26,620
but she is in a dilemma as to what to do.

293
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:29,465
She wants to have a family and have kids,

294
00:19:29,545 --> 00:19:34,160
but there is also a pressure that it comes with an expiry date.

295
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:39,910
And then her previous relationship which obviously has scarred her and everything.

296
00:19:39,990 --> 00:19:45,270
So, now she wants to ask if there should be a middle ground for this.

297
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:50,070
First of all, it's really good to hear that you're in therapy. I always always endorse that.

298
00:19:50,150 --> 00:19:52,408
Tomorrow is my turn at 2 o'clock.

299
00:19:52,488 --> 00:19:53,445
But it's okay.

300
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:55,714
I mean, it's a very good outlet.

301
00:19:55,794 --> 00:19:57,630
I cannot stress this enough.

302
00:19:57,710 --> 00:20:00,870
Okay, a lot of people ask for their therapist's number, they want to go there too.

303
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:01,950
It's not like that.

304
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:03,585
It's not sharing.

305
00:20:03,665 --> 00:20:06,618
I don't know man, I'm very secure about that.

306
00:20:06,698 --> 00:20:09,191
I don't know if that even makes sense.

307
00:20:09,271 --> 00:20:13,550
Even though I was recommended by someone I knew through someone.

308
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:16,051
So it doesn't make sense.

309
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:16,631
Anyway.

310
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:23,398
So your first relationship was at an immature age and as you said it doesn't count.

311
00:20:23,478 --> 00:20:25,519
So the first one is like that.

312
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:29,590
One is at an immature age and it's usually there to guide us.

313
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:43,590
Because in the first one, you like the songs of Mukaddar ka Sikandar and Sajan films.

314
00:20:43,670 --> 00:20:48,520
But then when you realize that it's not like that, it's a kick in the butt.

315
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:51,670
So it's very important to have that heartbreak.

316
00:20:55,220 --> 00:21:02,140
As you said, you were quite emotionally involved and you got cheated on twice.

317
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:09,140
Now what could be the reasons for that? I don't know. It was a long distance relationship for the most part.

318
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:16,140
Out of sight, out of mind, people do it. Although distance should create fondness and it should and it must.

319
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:20,930
But clearly, as you said, you were quite emotionally involved and you got cheated on twice.

320
00:21:21,010 --> 00:21:23,843
quite emotionally dependent on that person.

321
00:21:23,923 --> 00:21:28,010
So perhaps that person felt emotionally overwhelmed.

322
00:21:28,860 --> 00:21:32,428
I'm not justifying what he did was right.

323
00:21:32,508 --> 00:21:39,939
What I'm saying is that sometimes, as humans, and it goes for both men and women,

324
00:21:40,019 --> 00:21:48,250
we may not have to deal with our emotions and we put a lot of things on the other person.

325
00:21:48,950 --> 00:21:54,453
And then they emotionally feel the burden that this is too much.

326
00:21:54,533 --> 00:21:59,670
I need some space, I need some balance, I need my own things going on.

327
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:05,670
I mean, okay, you are a part of my life, but you're not my entire life. And that shouldn't happen either.

328
00:22:05,750 --> 00:22:09,189
What we say, you are my world, you are my universe, that's nonsense.

329
00:22:09,269 --> 00:22:14,750
You have to have your own space and you have to have your own hobbies and your own things that you.

330
00:22:15,340 --> 00:22:20,980
You should have your own space. I always endorse this.

331
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:25,220
So perhaps you didn't allow him that. I mean I'm just assuming. I didn't.

332
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,802
As you have written,

333
00:22:26,882 --> 00:22:34,980
it made you really needy because your parents didn't really give you that kind of affection.

334
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:42,150
So this is something to learn for parents and future parents that you really need to hug your child.

335
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:43,750
Like at least thrice a day.

336
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:45,345
Because he feels it.

337
00:22:45,425 --> 00:22:49,000
He says that in jokes, maybe you weren't hugged as a child.

338
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:51,920
So that's why you're behaving like this.

339
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,718
That's why you're frustrated.

340
00:22:53,798 --> 00:22:59,350
That's why you're full of hate towards other people because if only your father hugged you.

341
00:22:59,430 --> 00:23:03,361
They often taunt each other like this.

342
00:23:03,441 --> 00:23:05,668
But there is a wisdom in this.

343
00:23:05,748 --> 00:23:09,020
Wisdom means that I have to think in Hindi.

344
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:11,780
There is a wisdom in this.

345
00:23:11,860 --> 00:23:16,721
A child really looks up to his or her parents.

346
00:23:16,801 --> 00:23:19,966
Because they are his super heroes.

347
00:23:20,046 --> 00:23:24,301
When they appreciate, the child is so happy.

348
00:23:24,381 --> 00:23:27,080
He does that again and again.

349
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,588
So like my son likes to go around.

350
00:23:29,668 --> 00:23:32,293
So when we laugh, he goes around more.

351
00:23:32,373 --> 00:23:33,561
He enjoys it.

352
00:23:33,641 --> 00:23:37,210
But if you start scolding him, he would stop doing it.

353
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:40,210
And then he'll feel that maybe they don't like him.

354
00:23:40,290 --> 00:23:43,210
And then he'll find that affection somewhere else.

355
00:23:43,290 --> 00:23:48,210
And it's very natural. Humans, like, we eat food.

356
00:23:48,290 --> 00:23:53,210
I ate two chicken strips after the first question because I was hungry.

357
00:23:53,290 --> 00:23:58,210
So, like that is food, emotions are also human soul food.

358
00:23:58,290 --> 00:23:59,210
That's what I want.

359
00:23:59,290 --> 00:24:04,720
These hardcore people, I used to think last year that I could have lived alone.

360
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:12,220
I would chill, party, travel, why did I get married, this and that.

361
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:16,220
Sometimes I think about it, when I fight, I think about it.

362
00:24:16,300 --> 00:24:18,220
But then it doesn't happen.

363
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:23,720
I have seen a lot of people who had everything in life that you would want in your life.

364
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:27,220
What they didn't have was a relationship, they didn't have a family.

365
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:29,220
And I have seen them cry a lot.

366
00:24:29,300 --> 00:24:32,300
Because you can't eat money.

367
00:24:32,620 --> 00:24:36,080
You know, it's the, your need will be fulfilled.

368
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:42,160
Food and AC, you can do the comfort level, you can get the best bed in the world.

369
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:46,960
Like, there will be a water bed, a big AC, and cold air is also coming.

370
00:24:47,040 --> 00:24:51,660
But like, what good is all that when you don't have anyone around you?

371
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:56,760
So this is something that I also realized after COVID, you really need someone.

372
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:59,490
So, you're not wrong with that.

373
00:24:59,570 --> 00:25:00,770
But perhaps you overburdened him at some point.

374
00:25:00,850 --> 00:25:02,570
If you are in the day.

375
00:25:02,650 --> 00:25:06,210
Let's talk about the future now.

376
00:25:06,290 --> 00:25:09,050
You wrote that you have panic attacks at 9 AM.

377
00:25:09,130 --> 00:25:11,250
Now this is something alarming.

378
00:25:11,330 --> 00:25:15,490
Because how is the time set for this?

379
00:25:15,570 --> 00:25:18,090
Was it because of something you were eating?

380
00:25:18,170 --> 00:25:19,930
Or was it because of your dietary habits?

381
00:25:20,010 --> 00:25:26,170
Because if you have one time to eat, then you have only one time to wash.

382
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:32,680
Sometimes you're eating at 4, sometimes at 1, so your whole body is like this.

383
00:25:32,760 --> 00:25:39,000
So was it because you were eating something at some point which was leading to this? I am not sure.

384
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:43,181
Please, those who have gone through this or those who understand this,

385
00:25:43,261 --> 00:25:47,000
please tell us in the comments why this happened at exactly 9 PM.

386
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,760
I fail to understand this.

387
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:53,790
Or maybe, could it be because you're saying.

388
00:25:53,870 --> 00:26:00,850
You're saying it was usual time of call, meaning your doctor's call.

389
00:26:00,930 --> 00:26:06,850
Was it because of the anxiety at work or was it because of the pressure at work?

390
00:26:06,930 --> 00:26:10,430
Because that then it makes sense.

391
00:26:10,510 --> 00:26:15,410
That you had anxiety was leading to panic attack like symptoms.

392
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:19,680
I hope you don't get them anymore or you're not getting them anymore.

393
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:21,830
So there's nothing wrong.

394
00:26:21,910 --> 00:26:24,938
You said I was a strong independent woman in other's eyes,

395
00:26:25,018 --> 00:26:26,847
and there's nothing wrong with that.

396
00:26:26,927 --> 00:26:29,040
I would want you to continue to be that.

397
00:26:31,860 --> 00:26:38,700
You said that whenever I face any kind of emotional issues, I would run straight to him. That's perfectly fine.

398
00:26:38,780 --> 00:26:40,081
It's okay to be vulnerable.

399
00:26:40,161 --> 00:26:42,330
You can be the toughest cookie for the world,

400
00:26:42,410 --> 00:26:46,780
but it's okay to be vulnerable in front of your partner and that's what partners are for.

401
00:26:46,860 --> 00:26:50,970
You can be like the strongest warrior on the battlefield,

402
00:26:51,050 --> 00:26:55,585
but you also come home and hug someone and like to be pampered.

403
00:26:55,665 --> 00:26:57,220
That's perfectly fine.

404
00:26:58,830 --> 00:27:01,750
that I am something else for the world and you are something else for it.

405
00:27:01,830 --> 00:27:05,750
That's perfectly fine. Everybody is like that. I can assure you.

406
00:27:05,830 --> 00:27:09,750
People can come across like all rough and tough and you know,

407
00:27:09,830 --> 00:27:14,750
but from inside everyone has a heart, everyone is a human. So there is nothing wrong with that.

408
00:27:14,830 --> 00:27:20,830
Yes, so you are saying that your past experience of getting dependent on humans is starting to scare you.

409
00:27:21,830 --> 00:27:24,770
You cannot, so see.

410
00:27:25,140 --> 00:27:30,500
Every experience you'll have with people will be different one way or the other.

411
00:27:30,580 --> 00:27:36,540
Unless, I mean, you can't be doing the same things and expect different results.

412
00:27:36,620 --> 00:27:43,460
If you're going to be doing the same things that you were doing before, perhaps the results might be same.

413
00:27:43,810 --> 00:27:48,433
If you don't want your previous relationship to have a recap,

414
00:27:48,513 --> 00:27:53,020
or if it doesn't have an instant replay, then try it.

415
00:27:53,100 --> 00:28:01,020
So try not to do things that you'd like to think now were toxic or were something that you shouldn't have done.

416
00:28:01,100 --> 00:28:07,409
So sit and do an independent audit of your behavior, your emotions,

417
00:28:07,489 --> 00:28:10,020
that maybe I'm saying this thing.

418
00:28:10,100 --> 00:28:16,787
Or if you remember what he used to complain about you, like what are you doing,

419
00:28:16,867 --> 00:28:18,020
what did he say?

420
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:19,740
So like take that into consideration.

421
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:25,740
It's not necessary that he is right. It's not necessary that the complaints he made will be right. That's something that you need to figure out.

422
00:28:25,820 --> 00:28:30,845
Do a SWOT analysis and try not to do those things.

423
00:28:30,925 --> 00:28:35,472
And secondly, just because of one bad experience,

424
00:28:35,552 --> 00:28:40,820
you cannot label everyone that this will happen to everyone.

425
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:56,000
Finding the best people and sometimes these bad apples that we had in our lives were there so that we could appreciate the right ones.

426
00:28:56,080 --> 00:29:03,000
So, it is important to lose in life because winning gives you more flavor.

427
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,112
Similarly,

428
00:29:04,192 --> 00:29:12,720
having bad people in your life should not seize you or should not seize the idea of mingling with other people.

429
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:16,920
It should be there so that you learn something from it.

430
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:20,400
Try not to repeat those things that you think you shouldn't have done.

431
00:29:20,480 --> 00:29:27,193
And in the next round, if you find true love and if you find true happiness,

432
00:29:27,273 --> 00:29:30,080
you will appreciate it even more.

433
00:29:30,160 --> 00:29:35,174
So with this fear that because that was like this, so that will also be like this,

434
00:29:35,254 --> 00:29:37,030
this is not how life is lived.

435
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:39,320
And there is only one way to find out.

436
00:29:39,410 --> 00:29:40,126
I'm sorry,

437
00:29:40,206 --> 00:29:48,850
there's no guarantee that the next person will be the absolute perfect version of a man that should be.

438
00:29:48,930 --> 00:29:53,370
I'm not saying anything. There's no guarantee. There's only one way to find out.

439
00:29:53,450 --> 00:29:59,890
And that is, date that person and meet that person and try to talk to that person.

440
00:29:59,970 --> 00:30:03,730
Go out with him and try to see it for yourself.

441
00:30:03,810 --> 00:30:06,410
You have to do this yourself.

442
00:30:06,820 --> 00:30:11,907
In arranged marriage scenario, if you go, I don't know man,

443
00:30:11,987 --> 00:30:15,300
that's like the riskiest shit ever.

444
00:30:15,380 --> 00:30:16,882
Like it's so risky.

445
00:30:16,962 --> 00:30:24,079
We always tell our kids not to talk to any stranger and then get married to a stranger.

446
00:30:24,159 --> 00:30:25,739
Go have sex with him.

447
00:30:25,819 --> 00:30:26,530
Like why?

448
00:30:26,780 --> 00:30:32,260
So this is very off scene. So try not to do that.

449
00:30:33,110 --> 00:30:39,350
That's a gamble. That's like a literal gamble. You don't know how that person is.

450
00:30:39,430 --> 00:30:41,633
So do not stop yourself.

451
00:30:41,713 --> 00:30:44,946
And yes, as far as you want to travel and explore,

452
00:30:45,026 --> 00:30:48,026
take a month off or take a few weeks off.

453
00:30:48,106 --> 00:30:49,847
Go to Goa, go to other places.

454
00:30:49,927 --> 00:30:54,012
I don't know where you've been and I don't know where you want to go.

455
00:30:54,092 --> 00:30:55,899
Go out.

456
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:59,690
Like you, you, traveling is the best thing you can do to yourself.

457
00:30:59,770 --> 00:31:02,850
I cannot stress this enough and I'm sorry if a lot of those people who haven't traveled or don't have the means to travel are hating me right now.

458
00:31:02,930 --> 00:31:03,430
I worked my ass off and now it's happening.

459
00:31:04,930 --> 00:31:07,690
So I'm going to do.

460
00:31:07,770 --> 00:31:09,981
I also used to be that person.

461
00:31:10,061 --> 00:31:11,565
I used to aspire.

462
00:31:11,645 --> 00:31:16,819
I used to see my friends around who were in corporate jobs and were going to Taiwan,

463
00:31:16,899 --> 00:31:18,690
Singapore, Hong Kong for free.

464
00:31:18,770 --> 00:31:23,770
I was like, shit man, I need a job like that where I can sit in a plane with someone else's money.

465
00:31:28,160 --> 00:31:30,480
Formula One, on someone else's money.

466
00:31:30,560 --> 00:31:32,480
So yeah, that's the dream.

